Btrfs regression test scripts, intended for use with an OpenBSD QEMU VM running on a Linux host.

run-* scripts are entrypoints.

Chunk growth tests use four concurrent writers, 64 KiB writes, and fsync every
4 MiB. They still exhaust the initial data capacity and verify every sector
after remount. Use run_all.py --chunk-stress (or chunks.py --stress) for the
original 4 KiB writes and fsync every 512 KiB; large DUP fixtures can take many
minutes with that pattern.
